        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.marincountyvisitor.com/places-to-go/novato/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s name honors a Miwok leader who was baptized as Saint Novatus.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novato%2C_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Novato History Museum, housed in the 1850 Postmaster’s House, opened in 1976 after a community renovation.",
